# ===========================================================================
# 2. Frontend ownership — packages/twenty-front
#
# Teams are named after the product domains in packages/twenty-docs/user-guide/
# so docs, product and ownership share one vocabulary. Ordered broad -> narrow;
# a nested override placed above its parent rule silently does nothing.
#
# NOTE: these handles are placeholders. GitHub only routes review to teams that
# exist in the owning organisation — rename them to real teams (or use
# individual owners) before expecting them to do anything.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2a. Catch-all. Nothing under twenty-front is ever unowned: a module added next
#    quarter belongs to platform until a product team claims it, rather than
#    falling through to nobody.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/packages/twenty-front/                                          @twenty/frontend-platform

